BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:13@default
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Join Maine author, Brandon Ying Kit Boey, for a discussion on his writing process and his new book, Karma of the Sun."In the isolation of the Himalayas, the snows still fall, but they are tinged with the ash of a nuclear winter; the winds still blow, but they wail with the cry of ghosts. The seventh and final blast is near. As the world heaves its final breaths, the people of the Tibetan plateau&mdash;civilization&rsquo;s final survivors&mdash;are haunted by spirits and terrorized by warlords. Though the last of the seven prophesied cataclysms is at hand, young Karma searches for a father who disappeared ten years earlier, presumed dead. Driven by a yearning to see his father again before the end, and called by an eerie horn unheard by anyone else, Karma forges into the Himalayas and discovers that his father&rsquo;s disappearance may be linked to a mystical mountain said to connect the physical world with the spirit lands&mdash;and a possible way to save their doomed future."For more information about the book and author, please visit Boey's website!
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261111T111128Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20230202T000000Z
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20230202T010000Z
LOCATION:South Berwick Public Library
SUMMARY;LANGUAGE=en-us:Local Author Visit: Brandon Ying Kit Boey
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
