BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:119@default
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Mary S. BuildMary Build of Bridgton, Maine has recently been awarded the 2023 Award of Achievement for Contributions to Aviation by the International Organization of Women Pilots, The Ninety-Nines, Inc.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Mary has contributed to the Ninety-Nines on both the local and international levels of the organization and has just recently been voted in as one of two directors. She has just completed her second term as governor of the New England Section of the Ninety-Nines.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; A career pilot, flight instructor and former FAA Designated Pilot Examiner, she is also an FAA FAASTeam (safety) Representative. Her safety seminars have been presented on the national level. She is an accomplished air race competitor and judge. She is also the author of the book, Finding Myself In Aviation.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; She started flying when she was 47 and continued to add ratings over the years. She has flown scenic flights on floats taking over 1,000 passengers a year, started her own seaplane flight school and ran that for sixteen years. She is now teaching land operations in three airports, Portland, Fryeburg and Oxford, Maine.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; She will do a reading of what life was like as a married 23 year old with a young child. She will also talk about some of her adventures flying to Alaska and experiencing a seaplane accident.
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261111T111128Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20241016T220000Z
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20241016T230000Z
LOCATION:none
SUMMARY;LANGUAGE=en-us:Author Visit - Mary Build
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
