DESCRIPTION:&nbsp;Monica Wood.&nbsp; &nbsp;"How to Read a Book" and "When We Were the Kennedy's"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;How to Read a Book, her new novel, is the&nbsp;People&nbsp;Magazine&nbsp;book of the week and one of its "Best Books of May" selections&ldquo;A charming, deeply moving novel about second chances, unlikely friendships, and the life-changing power of sharing stories.&rdquo; (Goodreads.)The author of the best selling&nbsp;When We Were the Kennedys,&nbsp;a memoir of growing up in the paper mill town of Mexicon, Maine, Monica Wood is also a novelist and playwright. She is the 2024 recipient of the Sara Josepha Hale award for excellence in New England literary arts.
