DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a night of poetry!Mary McColley is a writer and poet originally from Maine. She has wandered and worked for several years in France, Thailand, and Palestine. Her work has appeared in the Paris/Atlantic literary journal, the Portland Press Herald, Maine Magazine, multiple anthologies of the Telling Room, and on public radio broadcasts. She also authored the mystery novel A Wrinkle in Crime. She enjoys running, languages, killing lobsters and selling street art.&nbsp;
