DESCRIPTION:Discover the birthplace of Disney&rsquo;s Bambi, the northern forest ice caves, abandoned railroads, petrographs, and tales which can only be described as &ldquo;classic Maine!"Tim Caverly has spent his life in Maine&rsquo;s outdoors. Growing up shadowing his father who was a fire warden with the Maine Forest Service and his brother, a ranger in Baxter State Park, it was natural for him to seek a career in the outdoors. Tim, along with his wife Susan and their Golden Retriever Sandi, travel all across New England to present programs encouraging literacy and discovery of New England&rsquo;s spectacular world.Tim will have books for sale and signing after the presentation.
