UID:217@default
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a cozy and cheerful way to celebrate Valentine&rsquo;s Day? Whether&nbsp;you&rsquo;re&nbsp;spending the evening on your own or with someone special, the South Berwick Public Library invites you to enjoy a free night of live music, community, and connection, sponsored by the Friends of the South Berwick Public Library.&nbsp;Join us on Friday, February 13,&nbsp;2026&nbsp;at 6:00 PM for a Valentine&rsquo;s Day Concert featuring local musicians June and the Honey Badgers. Known for their high-energy performances and playful use of ukuleles, the Honey Badgers are a 5-piece band that perform crowd-pleasing hits, making sure that everyone has a fun and memorable experience, whether&nbsp;they&rsquo;re&nbsp;dancing to the music, singing along, or just enjoying the groove.&nbsp;This evening is all about coming together and enjoying good company. The evening will include light refreshments, and enough fun to keep your heart warm all winter. Whether you settle in to listen or take time to mingle with friends and neighbors, we hope you&rsquo;ll feel right at home. All are welcome for this relaxed and heartwarming evening. We look forward to celebrating with you!
