DESCRIPTION:Kate Woodworth is the award-winning author of the novels&nbsp;Little Great Island&nbsp;and&nbsp;Racing into the Dark. She is also the creative force behind the grassroots climate change initiative, Be the Butterfly, that invites everyone to perform one small act to help mitigate climate change.&nbsp;Kate writes about the impact of climate change on our food supply on her Substack, &ldquo;Food in the Time of Climate Change.&rdquo; She has appeared on C-Span2 Book TV, NPR&rsquo;s Maine Calling, and Good Day, Maine. Her essays on climate fiction and the role of fiction writers in the climate discourse have been published by the Climate Fiction Writers League.&nbsp;Kate&rsquo;s book,&nbsp;Little Great Island, was selected for NPR&rsquo;s Maine Public Book Club for&nbsp;April,&nbsp;2026.&nbsp;Kate will be selling her books at this event!&nbsp;
