DESCRIPTION:We are pleased to welcome back EcoMaine for another informative program about recycling in our communities! "Wishcycling" - the practice of tossing materials in your recycling bin without knowing whether they are truly recyclable - has a lot of impacts on the recycling process. From plastic grocery bags, to Styrofoam, to loose bottle caps, commonly "wishcycled" items are easy to come by and confusing to dispose of. This presentation explores the ins and outs of recycling, the many impacts of &ldquo;wishcycling&rdquo; on the recycling process, a behind the scenes look at EcoMaine's single-sort recycling facility, and a glimpse of what's ahead. Attendees are invited to bring a mystery item to share!
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261111T111128Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260909T213000Z
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260909T223000Z
LOCATION:none
SUMMARY;LANGUAGE=en-us:EcoMaine Presents: "Wishcycling"
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
