UID:292@default
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a very special Halloween program with author and medium Rob Gutro! Experience a public paranormal investigation at the Hunt Memorial Library in Nashua, NH with Rob and Monique Toosoon. Their findings revealed three ghosts that were not associated with the building but chose the building as their residence. Together with other paranormal professionals and members of the public, they uncovered a haunted secret love, illicit trysts, a ghostly teenage accident victim, and haunted paintings. &nbsp;&nbsp; In the Ghosts of Linville Manor &ndash; Maryland&rsquo;s Most Haunted House, Rob&rsquo;s investigation revealed the identities of several ghosts, including one who remains there due to being unjustly accused. This book details that investigation, provides a glimpse of the home's past, and shares many of the supernatural interactions people have experienced. This event is bound to be a very ghostly encounter!
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261111T111128Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261021T213000Z
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261021T223000Z
LOCATION:none
SUMMARY;LANGUAGE=en-us:The Many Ghosts of a NH Library and a Maryland Manor House with medium Rob Gutro
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:293@default
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Generative AI is everywhere. This workshop will cover the basics of how this technology works, why it is unreliable as a source of information, and the privacy, social, and environmental concerns associated with AI. Resources will be provided on how to disable AI on your devices or seek out alternatives. If you are curious about large language models and artificial intelligence, or you are suspicious of how this technology is being pushed out, join our library director Melissa to learn more.
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261111T111128Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260929T220000Z
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260929T230000Z
LOCATION:none
SUMMARY;LANGUAGE=en-us:Why Avoid AI?
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:294@default
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:The Governor has tasked the Maine State Library with building a statewide plan for AI literacy and safety. &nbsp;As a first step, the Maine State Library&rsquo;s project team is traveling across the state to host a series of community conversations.&nbsp; South Berwick has been chosen to host one of these conversations on Friday, October 2nd from 12-1pm at the South Berwick Public Library at 27 Young Street.The state library is looking for broad input from people in fields that include healthcare, business, journalism government, farming, education, the arts and more.The goal is to learn directly from Maine residents: How are Mainers actually using AI (key themes include healthcare, education, workforce/economy)? What questions, concerns, and opportunities are coming up, and what do people want to know? And how can libraries and other local organizations support people to use it wisely and advance their goals?&nbsp; What is learned will shape the Maine AI Literacy and Safety Framework, which will be published by the end of 2026.&nbsp;If you are able to attend, please RSVP to me at mrobinson@southberwicklibrary.org or 207-384-3308.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261111T111128Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261002T160000Z
DTEND;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261002T170000Z
LOCATION:none
SUMMARY;LANGUAGE=en-us:Maine State Library Listening Tour: AI Literacy and Safety
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
