DESCRIPTION:The Seacoast Ukulele Players are an informal group of ukulele players that has met weekly at the Seabrook Library since 2017. They will provide a comfortable, friendly, and fun environment in which to share their favorite songs and strengthen their skills together.&nbsp;SUP plays everything from 1930&rsquo;s standards to rock and roll; their favorite genre is popular hits of the 60&rsquo;s and 70&rsquo;s, and we are prone to throw in some of our own parodies of familiar tunes. What they may lack in finesse they make up for with fun! This is bound to be a joyous performance! This event is open to all ages.
